# CYS-RVC — Cys-S to ketone/aldehyde reversible covalent adduct (hemithioketal)
#
# Hand-authored link CIF for PyKeko covalent-ligand workflow.
# Family F6 of the plan-doc taxonomy: covers warheads that form a
# REVERSIBLE covalent bond with Cys-S — typically reactive carbonyls
# (ketones, aldehydes) yielding a tetrahedral hemithioketal at the
# attack site. Boronate warheads (bortezomib-class) form an analogous
# B-S linkage but the boronate chemistry is distinct enough to need
# its own link CIF (CYS-BRC.cif, not shipped in v0.2.32).
#
# Mechanism:
#   R-C(=O)-R'  +  Cys-S⁻  ⇌  R-C(OH)(S-Cys)-R'  (sp³, tetrahedral)
#
# The bond IS reversible — the equilibrium favours the hemithioketal
# in the binding pocket (where the local Cys-S concentration is high
# and the carbonyl is positioned by other binding interactions) but
# the bond can break under different conditions. For refmacat modelling
# we treat it as a snapshot: the bound state is what we refine; the
# reversibility is a binding-energetics property, not a structural one.
#
# Differences vs F1/F3/F5 (sp3 thioether amide chemistries):
#   * No amide N — the carbonyl is a ketone/aldehyde, not an amide.
#     This is the detector's distinguishing signature: Cβ has =O but
#     NO N neighbour.
#   * Cβ retypes sp2 → sp3 (was carbonyl, becomes tetrahedral).
#   * The carbonyl-O becomes -OH on Cβ (not on a separate Cα as in F4
#     epoxide). The O stays on the same atom; just the bond order
#     and one new H change.
#
# PLACEHOLDER TOKENS substituted at runtime:
#   <LIG> ← ligand 3-letter (or 5-char) CCD code
#   <CB>  ← Cβ atom-id (the C that takes the SG; was the carbonyl C)
#   <O>   ← the (formerly carbonyl, now hydroxyl) O atom-id
#   <HO>  ← H to add on the O (the hemithioketal hydroxyl H)
#   <HCB> ← H to delete on Cβ (post-product input only; only if Cβ
#            was uploaded with an explicit spare H to delete, which is
#            rare for hemithioketal form since Cβ usually keeps its
#            two original substituents)
#
# References:
#   ~/Moorhen/docs/refs/nicholls-modelling-2021.pdf — CCP4-ML link-CIF format
#   ~/Moorhen/docs/covalent-ligand-plan.md §2.6 (F6 reversible carbonyl family)

data_link_CYS-RVC
_chem_link.id                CYS-RVC
_chem_link.name              "Cys-S to ketone/aldehyde reversible adduct (hemithioketal)"
_chem_link.comp_id_1         CYS
_chem_link.mod_id_1          CYS-RVC-mod1
_chem_link.group_comp_1      L-peptide
_chem_link.comp_id_2         <LIG>
_chem_link.mod_id_2          CYS-RVC-mod2
_chem_link.group_comp_2      non-polymer

# ---- bonds: new S-Cβ single bond (sp3 S to sp3 C) ----
loop_
_chem_link_bond.atom_1_comp_id
_chem_link_bond.atom_id_1
_chem_link_bond.atom_2_comp_id
_chem_link_bond.atom_id_2
_chem_link_bond.type
_chem_link_bond.value_dist
_chem_link_bond.value_dist_esd
 1 SG    2 <CB>   single 1.83 0.03

# ---- angles around the new sp3 hemithioketal ----
# Cys side: standard sp3 thioether range, slightly wider σ because
# the hemithioketal is more strained electronically than a simple
# sp3 thioether.
# Ligand side: SG-Cβ-O ~109° (tetrahedral with one polar substituent).
loop_
_chem_link_angle.atom_1_comp_id
_chem_link_angle.atom_id_1
_chem_link_angle.atom_2_comp_id
_chem_link_angle.atom_id_2
_chem_link_angle.atom_3_comp_id
_chem_link_angle.atom_id_3
_chem_link_angle.value_angle
_chem_link_angle.value_angle_esd
 1 CB    1 SG    2 <CB>   100.0   4.0
 1 SG    2 <CB>  2 <O>    109.0   3.0

# ---- soft torsion ----
loop_
_chem_link_tor.id
_chem_link_tor.atom_1_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_1
_chem_link_tor.atom_2_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_2
_chem_link_tor.atom_3_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_3
_chem_link_tor.atom_4_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_4
_chem_link_tor.value_angle
_chem_link_tor.value_angle_esd
_chem_link_tor.period
 sp3_sp3_cys_hinge 1 CA    1 CB    1 SG    2 <CB>   180.0  25.0  3


# =====================================================================
# Cys-side modification: delete HG (the thiol H)
# =====================================================================
data_mod_CYS-RVC-mod1
loop_
_chem_mod_atom.mod_id
_chem_mod_atom.function
_chem_mod_atom.atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_symbol
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_energy
_chem_mod_atom.new_partial_charge
 CYS-RVC-mod1 delete HG . . . .


# =====================================================================
# Ligand-side modification — POST-PRODUCT HEMITHIOKETAL INPUT BRANCH.
#
# User uploaded a ligand where the hemithioketal is already drawn —
# Cβ has S, OH, R, R'. No structural changes needed (Cβ already sp3,
# already has the right neighbours). The minimal mod2 is empty.
#
# If the runtime detector instead matched the carbonyl pre-reaction
# form (free drug SMILES with C=O), use CYS-RVC-mod2-carbonyl.cif
# which:
#   (1) changes the C=O bond from double to single
#   (2) retypes Cβ from sp2 (CR1 / C carbonyl) to sp3 (CT)
#   (3) adds an H on the O (the hemithioketal hydroxyl H)
# =====================================================================
data_mod_CYS-RVC-mod2
loop_
_chem_mod_atom.mod_id
_chem_mod_atom.function
_chem_mod_atom.atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_symbol
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_energy
_chem_mod_atom.new_partial_charge
# No-op: F6 post-product (hemithioketal) input requires no atom changes
# on the ligand. Cβ in the saturated form already has the correct bond
# list. Empty loop_ block kept for parser-compatibility.
